1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,646
Most pharmacies still run on fax machines, phone calls, paper logs, and systems that don't talk to each other.

2
00:00:05,646 --> 00:00:09,212
The lot, the patient, and the prescription live in three different places.

3
00:00:09,272 --> 00:00:12,481
Chimera Rx shows what a modern pharmacy system looks like.

4
00:00:12,481 --> 00:00:18,257
One connected ledger links every lot, every patient, and every prescription, from the dock to the pickup counter.

5
00:00:18,317 --> 00:00:19,822
Here's a quick tour, by role.

6
00:00:19,882 --> 00:00:21,360
The technician receives a delivery.

7
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:27,274
Scan the label, and the lot gate checks the paperwork, the expiry, and the recall list before stock is shelved.

8
00:00:27,334 --> 00:00:34,929
The pharmacist sees inventory by lot, with expiry and shelf location, then fills and verifies each order, with Rx Watcher checking the rules.

9
00:00:34,989 --> 00:00:39,004
The cashier runs pickup and the register, and can't see allergies or recalls.

10
00:00:39,064 --> 00:00:43,003
Refills show who is due, and patients keep their full history in one place.

11
00:00:43,063 --> 00:00:44,801
Here's the gap old systems leave.

12
00:00:44,801 --> 00:00:49,435
A recall fax arrives, and nobody captured the lot, so you warn everyone, or no one.

13
00:00:49,495 --> 00:00:50,889
Connected, it takes seconds.

14
00:00:50,889 --> 00:00:57,509
The pharmacist confirms the lots, stock moves to quarantine, and the exact patients appear, with messages drafted for approval.

15
00:00:57,569 --> 00:00:59,222
Everything speaks open standards.

16
00:00:59,222 --> 00:01:06,663
DSCSA traceability and EPCIS exports give every package a history, and the sandbox verifier flags a spoofed one.

17
00:01:06,723 --> 00:01:11,537
Partners connect through a REST API, an MCP server, FHIR behind OAuth, and signed webhooks.

18
00:01:11,537 --> 00:01:15,068
The admin controls who gets in, and every call is audited.

19
00:01:15,128 --> 00:01:18,698
Two stores can transfer stock, and both audit logs record the move.

20
00:01:18,758 --> 00:01:27,183
Real-world connections are designed seams: text messages, email, phone calls, wholesaler, e-prescribing, the dispensing system, the EHR, payer, SSO, and key management.

21
00:01:27,183 --> 00:01:31,012
They are sandboxed today, so nothing reaches a real person.

22
00:01:31,072 --> 00:01:32,302
Now the AI agents.

23
00:01:32,302 --> 00:01:39,070
Eight of them help in the background: a recall reader, an order watcher, a guardian, outreach drafters, a night digest, and more.

24
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:40,915
Every one follows the same rule.

25
00:01:40,915 --> 00:01:45,222
Rules decide, the model explains, a gate checks the model, and a pharmacist decides.

26
00:01:45,282 --> 00:01:50,365
Rx Guardian works on its own, even when nobody is looking, and it never changes an order itself.

27
00:01:50,365 --> 00:01:56,013
Run it now, and it flags things a busy pharmacist could miss, like duplicate therapy, an interaction, or late fills.

28
00:01:56,073 --> 00:01:58,638
Each suggestion shows its evidence from the patient's history.

29
00:01:58,638 --> 00:02:03,482
Accept one, and the order goes on hold with the reason recorded, so the pharmacist can decide.

30
00:02:03,482 --> 00:02:05,762
Dismiss it, and the reason is kept too.

31
00:02:05,822 --> 00:02:11,716
The Coroner keeps only lots printed word for word on the recall notice, and drops anything the model invented.

32
00:02:11,716 --> 00:02:19,782
Outreach drafts for recalls and refills need the pharmacist's attestation before anything is sent, and a patient on a recalled lot never gets a routine reminder.

33
00:02:19,842 --> 00:02:23,687
Pick any provider: Bedrock, Anthropic, an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or a local model.

34
00:02:23,687 --> 00:02:28,494
Patient names and birth dates stay out of the prompts, and every run is logged.

35
00:02:28,554 --> 00:02:30,011
Security is built in.

36
00:02:30,011 --> 00:02:35,837
PHI fields are encrypted, roles are enforced on the server, and the audit log is hash-chained.

37
00:02:35,837 --> 00:02:38,022
These are HIPAA-style safeguards, not certified.

38
00:02:38,082 --> 00:02:38,917
Built with Kiro.

39
00:02:38,917 --> 00:02:43,648
Specs carry requirement IDs, steering holds the safety rules, and hooks run a PHI guard on save.

40
00:02:43,648 --> 00:02:48,380
A custom agent and a Kiro Crew team did the work, with a human at every gate.

41
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,349
Chimera Rx.

42
00:02:49,349 --> 00:02:51,167
github.com/pjborad/Chimera-Rx.

43
00:02:51,167 --> 00:02:52,985
pjborad.github.io/Chimera-Rx.

44
00:02:52,985 --> 00:02:54,348
Synthetic data only.

